Janis Papanagnou wrote:
> Instead of writing more than one Elbereth in one attempt (which can require
> more than one turn), write Elbereth, then add Elbereth to existing writing,
> and add more as desired. That way you are guaranteed that you can completely
> write each word in one turn.

Writing two Elbereths costs only one turn, which is why it's sometimes
faster. However, it doesn't protect you for the turn you write it, and
nor do any existing Elbereths on the square. Writing one at a time costs
one action (which can be faster than one turn if you have speed), but
protects you on the monster turn if it's successful, and doesn't disrupt
existing Elbereths.

